  "id": "1st-official-pokemon-card-game-tournament",
  "name": "1st Official Pokémon Card Game Tournament",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The first official Pokémon Card Game tournament was held on 14 and 15 June 1997 at Makuhari Messe in Chiba, as part of the 6th Next Generation World Hobby Fair. Its 1,000 players, children up to 15, were picked by lottery, and it ran as four single-elimination sessions over the two days. Each session's top players got a cosmos holo trophy card in an acrylic stand and a champion's cap: No. 1 for the winner and No. 2 for the runner-up, four of each, and No. 3 for both third and fourth place.\n\nMitsuhiro Arita drew Pikachu holding a gold trophy, a silver trophy or a bronze cup. The text says that by showing the card you may enter the Pokémon Card Game Official Tournament ahead of others. The same art was printed again for the Lizardon and Kamex Mega Battle trophies, which change only that sentence, so these first cards are often confused with them.",
    "sources": [
